// OpenRC Simulator - Biplane 1300.
//
// The fifth aeroplane, and the first that is not a monoplane. What makes it
// different is not the second wing on its own but three things together:
//
//   BIPLANE INTERFERENCE. Each wing flies in the other's upwash and downwash,
//   so the pair behaves like one wing of far lower aspect ratio than either
//   has geometrically - 7.6 apiece becomes about 4.4 between them. That is
//   where a biplane's drag really comes from, not from the struts alone.
//
//   FOUR AILERONS. Both wings carry them, which is why a Pitts rolls the way
//   it does and why this is the fastest-rolling aeroplane in the roster.
//
//   SHORT COUPLED, TAIL-DRAGGER. A short tail arm and no nose wheel: it needs
//   flying in pitch the whole time and it will try to swap ends on the ground.
//
// validation_targets are MEASURED, not asserted - see Trainer1500.json.
